(2327795, 319281, 30454, '<td valign="top">WTG, Amy. Very nice composition, like the colors. The duotone works perfect here for the Chrome challenge. 26th place really great. Congratulations!!</td>', 'WTG, Amy. Very nice composition, like the colors. The duotone works perfect here for the Chrome challenge. 26th place really great. Congratulations!!', '2006-04-19 23:42:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328289, 319796, 55749, '<td valign="top">My photo had several issues to contend with.  First, I didn''t brew enough coffee to get the pour to flow properly through the nozzle.  So I added water... Bad choice, I should have brewed more coffee, instead the coffee looked more like tea.  Secondly, my six foot wide white paper blind looks like a postage stamp on the nozzle.  Oh if I could have used "advanced" photoshop technics to blend it away.  I went with a blue background because my original thought was to make a black and white image.  However, the coffee wasn''t dark enough to stand out in B&amp;W.  So. in the end, I rather liked the red handle, so I went with color.  Yes, its slightly over sharpened... I like that effect on metal.  However, notice that it doesn''t effect the color channels only the luminance.  Can you guess how I did that? Oh well, I''m happy with my placing.  TTFN</td>', 'My photo had several issues to contend with.  First, I didn''t brew enough coffee to get the pour to flow properly through the nozzle.  So I added water... Bad choice, I should have brewed more coffee, instead the coffee looked more like tea.  Secondly, my six foot wide white paper blind looks like a postage stamp on the nozzle.  Oh if I could have used "advanced" photoshop technics to blend it away.  I went with a blue background because my original thought was to make a black and white image.  However, the coffee wasn''t dark enough to stand out in B&W.  So. in the end, I rather liked the red handle, so I went with color.  Yes, its slightly over sharpened... I like that effect on metal.  However, notice that it doesn''t effect the color channels only the luminance.  Can you guess how I did that? Oh well, I''m happy with my placing.  TTFN', '2006-04-20 01:50:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2328409, 320047, 46448, '<td valign="top">Shannon, You could have done this with the glowing red eye dude! I know you have the talent to pull that off. I Like this its great, but dang dude if your going for the gusto for terminated It could have had more cowbell! Congrates on the Red, just wish ya to blue!</td>', 'Shannon, You could have done this with the glowing red eye dude! I know you have the talent to pull that off. I Like this its great, but dang dude if your going for the gusto for terminated It could have had more cowbell! Congrates on the Red, just wish ya to blue!', '2006-04-20 02:51:46.000000', NULL, 0),
