(2338387, 319953, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I think we had one of these when I was a kid .. the same light blue colour as well.  You have mentioned you are disapointed with how you did .. I took a look at what beat you out .. and they aren''t other rusty car pics .. on a whole they are shiny new crome things ...<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I really don''t mind this composition .. take a look at those that did better the new ones showed parts and the old stuff seemed to show more complete images ... this to me has a good balance .. I would have like slightly more at the top with the badge hitting horizontal thirds ... try different crops again .. and see if any work better that is the way to learn.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge with excessive force!<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I like the natural light and I love that the crome is not blown ... technically a good "solid" shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Try different cropping and learn to read the minds of the voters ... we all have trouble with that ... lots of the time.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Don''t be disappointed ... it takes too much energy ... just go and do better next time .. and if not then the time after ... I love your portfolio .. and your work .. keep it up!<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. First Impression - the most important one: I think we had one of these when I was a kid .. the same light blue colour as well.  You have mentioned you are disapointed with how you did .. I took a look at what beat you out .. and they aren''t other rusty car pics .. on a whole they are shiny new crome things ... Composition: I really don''t mind this composition .. take a look at those that did better the new ones showed parts and the old stuff seemed to show more complete images ... this to me has a good balance .. I would have like slightly more at the top with the badge hitting horizontal thirds ... try different crops again .. and see if any work better that is the way to learn. Subject: Meets the challenge with excessive force! Technical (Colour and light): I like the natural light and I love that the crome is not blown ... technically a good "solid" shot. To grow its vote?: Try different cropping and learn to read the minds of the voters ... we all have trouble with that ... lots of the time. Summary: Don''t be disappointed ... it takes too much energy ... just go and do better next time .. and if not then the time after ... I love your portfolio .. and your work .. keep it up! If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 05:20:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338403, 317356, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.  I think you drew the short straw and got me again ... here goes ...<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>I think this is so funky!  You have done well and I think this has appealed to a good range on the voters.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>It seems a little cut off on the left ... but I like the way that this works ... it would be hard to change without skewing the picture more.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>meets and excels at this challenge!<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Colours and DOF work really well ... it should say the aperture in the exif data on your JPG ... or the properties of the original pic.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>This is an above average shot giving true insight into the mind and room of a young photographer .. I think sharing this may have been a little nerveracking .. .cos I don''t know that I could ... It is hard when some voters are not able to see the value of a picture.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Sorry about your dog ... but I am sure you have many pics to remind you of him ... keep up the shooting you are always improving and challenging yourself which is good to see.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.  I think you drew the short straw and got me again ... here goes ... First Impression - the most important one: I think this is so funky!  You have done well and I think this has appealed to a good range on the voters. Composition: It seems a little cut off on the left ... but I like the way that this works ... it would be hard to change without skewing the picture more. Subject: meets and excels at this challenge! Technical (Colour and light): Colours and DOF work really well ... it should say the aperture in the exif data on your JPG ... or the properties of the original pic. To grow its vote?: This is an above average shot giving true insight into the mind and room of a young photographer .. I think sharing this may have been a little nerveracking .. .cos I don''t know that I could ... It is hard when some voters are not able to see the value of a picture. Summary: Sorry about your dog ... but I am sure you have many pics to remind you of him ... keep up the shooting you are always improving and challenging yourself which is good to see. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-04-24 05:46:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338438, 319147, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/>It is fine to leave information in the comments post a challenge, but to get the feel of what the picture is set up to convey etc should be entered at the time of the entry .. so that this can be taken into account when critiquing .. this is perhaps my challenge to you for future entries.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge ... but seems to be a little flat.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I think this works reasoanbly well.  Seems  to meet the rule of thirds ... I really do like the reflections .. the curviture in the hubs works well to double them out.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge .. with a reasonable amount of gusto.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is ok in this shot .. but I prefer the colurs in the other shot ... the cars also appear crisper in that shot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>If another shot is better enter it.  Wasting peoples time by saying you are "testing a site'' gives the impression that you don''t seem to care when the best shot is not entered.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>If you look at those who win they recieve a lot of comments, but also so do those who come last .. and the DQs get the most.  Take it as it comes.  I believe by leading by example .. I don''t always have time to comment but take my turn at critiquing ... this is a great way for people to learn ... why don''t you join and utilise that opportunity too.<br/> <br/>This is a good solid shot, I think we are to see more and better from you if DPC has passed your challenge ... if not good luck.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari<br/> <br/>Edited to add:  Voting is annonomus .. no one knows whose pics they are voting on or what they are scoring ... so comparing your comments with another long term users is a ridiculas comparison.  (just registered from your note below)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-24 05:35:41.</i></td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. It is fine to leave information in the comments post a challenge, but to get the feel of what the picture is set up to convey etc should be entered at the time of the entry .. so that this can be taken into account when critiquing .. this is perhaps my challenge to you for future entries. First Impression - the most important one: Meets the challenge ... but seems to be a little flat. Composition: I think this works reasoanbly well.  Seems  to meet the rule of thirds ... I really do like the reflections .. the curviture in the hubs works well to double them out. Subject: Meets the challenge .. with a reasonable amount of gusto. Technical (Colour and light): This is ok in this shot .. but I prefer the colurs in the other shot ... the cars also appear crisper in that shot. To grow its vote?: If another shot is better enter it.  Wasting peoples time by saying you are "testing a site'' gives the impression that you don''t seem to care when the best shot is not entered. Summary: If you look at those who win they recieve a lot of comments, but also so do those who come last .. and the DQs get the most.  Take it as it comes.  I believe by leading by example .. I don''t always have time to comment but take my turn at critiquing ... this is a great way for people to learn ... why don''t you join and utilise that opportunity too. This is a good solid shot, I think we are to see more and better from you if DPC has passed your challenge ... if not good luck. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari Edited to add:  Voting is annonomus .. no one knows whose pics they are voting on or what they are scoring ... so comparing your comments with another long term users is a ridiculas comparison.  (just registered from your note below)', '2006-04-24 06:11:16.000000', '2006-04-24 06:35:41.000000', 0),
